WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
A 0.9 kg weight pulls on the grasped object.
The attachment point is unknown to both estimators.

00:03.000 --> 00:08.000
One measurement leaves possible attachment points
along the force line of action.

00:08.000 --> 00:11.000
APCL restores candidate positions
along the unresolved direction.

00:11.000 --> 00:18.000
Tilt the object while keeping the cable attached.
The force direction changes in object coordinates.

00:18.000 --> 00:24.000
Let the load settle, then measure again.
Combine both views to narrow down the attachment point.

00:24.000 --> 00:30.000
This example: CPF 22.5 mm / APCL 8.7 mm position error.
Gold marks the true attachment; diamonds show the estimates.
